    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. u mentioned the \"political collapse\" and \"extremist groups\" as the reasons people call it a failure. but if the goal was specifically to prevent a massacre in Benghazi and stop Gaddafi, did the intervention actually achieve its primary moral and humanitarian objective? or does the chaos that followed just make the whole thing a wash regardless of what happened in Benghazi?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
