      "content": "that's a bit of a cop-out answer lol. it feels like ur trying to have it both ways. if the intervention's main legacy is basically just a failed state and a power vacuum in north africa, isn't it more accurate to say the strategy itself was flawed from the start? like, can we really call an intervention a \"success\" if it creates a massive regional security problem?",
